  "CardHelpSection": {
    "ParentObjectID": "advanced_copper_tools_large_saw",
    "LocalizationKey": "Advanced_Copper_Tools_LargeSaw_CardHelpSection",
    "DefaultText": "<b>Crafted:</b> From 3 metal sheets of one metal, 2 Wood, 2 copper nails and 1 tin solder using a hammer. The saw is the metal of its sheets.\n\n<b>Uses:</b> Cuts large trees faster than an axe while sharp. Copper, Ghost Bronze and Tin Bronze fell a large pine or willow in two pulls and a large birch or oak in three; White Bronze fells a pine or willow in one pull and a birch or oak in two; Tin takes two pulls for a pine, willow or birch and three for an oak. Each pull adds 1 Dullness; at 25 the saw is blunt and cuts like an axe until you drag a stone or whetstone onto it to sharpen it. A saw lasts about 100 pulls in copper, 166 in Ghost Bronze, 66 in Tin, 200 in Tin Bronze and 80 in White Bronze. Use as a cutting tool."
  },
